{"book":56,"chapter":1,"context":{"chapter":1,"title":"Elders for Crete","summary":"Paul reminds Titus to appoint elders of proven character in every town and to firmly correct the deceivers who were upsetting families with false teaching for profit.","background":"Paul uses 'elder' and 'bishop' (overseer) for the same leaders (vv. 5–7). He quotes a Cretan poet: 'The Cretians are alway liars, evil beasts, slow bellies' (v. 12); the line has traditionally been attributed to Epimenides, a Cretan of the sixth century BC. Cretans had such a reputation that Greeks used a verb meaning 'to act like a Cretan' for lying.","customs":[{"term":"Steward of God","verses":"1:7","note":"A steward managed a household for its owner. An elder manages God's household, the church, and must be trustworthy."}],"watchFor":["God 'that cannot lie' (v. 2) stands in contrast to the liars Paul describes.","'Unto the pure all things are pure' (v. 15).","Professing to know God but denying him by deeds (v. 16)."],"connections":["1 Timothy 3:1-7","Acts 14:23","Acts 27:7-13","Galatians 2:3"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["Παῦλος","Paulos","G3972","N-NSM-P","Paul"],["δοῦλος","doulos","G1401","N-NSM","a servant"],["θεοῦ","theou","G2316","N-GSM-T","of God"],["ἀπόστολος","apostolos","G652","N-NSM","an apostle"],["δὲ","de","G1161","CONJ","now"],["Ἰησοῦ","Iēsou","G2424","N-GSM-P","of Jesus"],["Χριστοῦ","Christou","G5547","N-GSM-T","Christ"],["κατὰ","kata","G2596","PREP","according to"],["πίστιν","pistin","G4102","N-ASF","[the] faith"],["ἐκλεκτῶν","eklektōn","G1588","A-GPM","of [the] elect"],["θεοῦ","theou","G2316","N-GSM-T","of God"],["καὶ","kai","G2532","CONJ","and"],["ἐπίγνωσιν","epignōsin","G1922","N-ASF","knowledge"],["ἀληθείας","alētheias","G225","N-GSF","of [the] truth"],["τῆς","tēs","G3588","T-GSF","which [is]"],["κατ᾽","kat᾽","G2596","PREP","according to"],["εὐσέβειαν","eusebeian","G2150","N-ASF","godliness"]],"x":[[45001001,45001001,16],[54006003,54006003,15],[55002023,55002023,10],[55002025,55002025,10]